<title>FRANCE: CIC ups Eurotunnel provisioning.</title>
<headline>CIC ups Eurotunnel provisioning.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>French bank CIC said on Tuesday it had raised its provisioning coverage on 900 million francs of subordinated Eurotunnel debt to 50 percent in the first half of 1996 from 30 percent at the end of 1995.</p>
<p>Chairman Bernard Yoncourt gave the detail on provisioning for troubled Anglo-French Channel Tunnel operator Eurotunnel at a CIC results news conference.</p>
<p>He said provisioning for exposure to Eurotunnel debt had been made to the tune of 30 percent in the second half of 1995 and then raised to 50 percent in the first half of this year.</p>
<p>He did not elaborate.</p>
</text>
